<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ r.title }}</title>
<style>
@page { size: A4; margin: 14mm 12mm; }
body { font-family: "DejaVu Sans", Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5px; color: #1b1b1b; max-width: 1050px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 12px; }
h1 { font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 2px; } h2 { font-size: 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 3px; margin-top: 22px; }
h3 { font-size: 12px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 6px 0 10px; font-size: 9.5px; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #d6d6d6; padding: 3px 5px; text-align: right; } th { background: #f2f2f2; }
td.l, th.l { text-align: left; }
.box { border: 1px solid #c9a227; background: #fff9e6; padding: 8px 10px; margin: 8px 0; }
.research { border: 1px dashed #888; background: #f7f7f7; padding: 8px 10px; }
.sev-high { color: #b00020; font-weight: bold; } .sev-medium { color: #a15c00; } .sev-low, .sev-info { color: #555; }
img { width: 100%; page-break-inside: avoid; } .muted { color: #666; } code { font-size: 9px; }
</style></head><body>
<h1>{{ r.title }}</h1>
<div class="muted">QuantEval v{{ r.quanteval_version }} &middot; run <code>{{ r.run_id }}</code> &middot; generated {{ r.started_at_utc[:19] }} UTC</div>

<div class="box"><b>Research evaluation only.</b> This report measures statistical properties of forecasting models on
historical OHLCV data supplied for the evaluation. It is not investment advice, makes no statement about any security's
future price, and contains no instructions to trade. Simulated historical results (section 6) depend on stated cost and
execution assumptions and do not indicate future results.</div>

<h2>1. Executive summary</h2>
<ul>{% for line in summary %}<li>{{ line | safe }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>

<h2>2. Data card</h2>
<table>
<tr><th class="l">File</th><td class="l">{{ r.data.path.split('/')[-1] }}</td><th class="l">SHA-256</th><td class="l"><code>{{ r.data.sha256 }}</code></td></tr>
<tr><th class="l">Instrument</th><td class="l">{{ r.data.symbol or 'n/a' }}</td><th class="l">Rows</th><td class="l">{{ r.data.rows }}</td></tr>
<tr><th class="l">Span (UTC)</th><td class="l">{{ r.data.start[:10] }} &rarr; {{ r.data.end[:10] }}</td><th class="l">Bar spacing</th><td class="l">{{ r.data.frequency }} (median {{ (r.data.bar_seconds/3600)|round(2) }} h){% if r.data.has_weekend_bars %}, includes weekend bars{% endif %}</td></tr>
<tr><th class="l">Columns</th><td class="l">{{ r.data.columns|join(', ') }}</td><th class="l">Provenance</th><td class="l">{{ r.data_provenance or 'not stated' }}</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>3. Protocol</h2>
<ul>
<li>Expanding-window walk-forward: {{ r.folds.n }} origins from {{ r.folds.first_origin_ts[:10] }} to {{ r.folds.last_origin_ts[:10] }}, step {{ r.folds.step }} bars (evaluation windows do not overlap), embargo {{ r.folds.embargo_bars }} bar(s) on parameter estimation, minimum history {{ r.config.min_history }} bars.</li>
<li>At each origin every model receives only bars up to and including the origin; forecasts cover the next {{ r.config.horizon }} bars of <i>close</i>. Future timestamps given to Kronos are generated from the bar calendar, not read from the file.</li>
<li>Models:<ul>{% for m in r.models %}<li><b>{{ m.name }}</b>: {{ m.description }}{% if m.model_revision %} &mdash; weights <code>{{ m.model_id }}@{{ m.model_revision[:7] }}</code>, tokenizer <code>{{ m.tokenizer_id }}@{{ m.tokenizer_revision[:7] }}</code>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></li>
<li>Metrics: MAE / RMSE / MAPE over all {{ r.config.horizon }} steps; relative MAE vs naive; Diebold-Mariano test on squared errors at bar {{ r.config.horizon }} vs naive; directional accuracy of the bar-{{ r.config.horizon }} move with Wilson 95% CI and a two-sided binomial test vs 50% (origins where the model or the market shows no change are excluded).</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Forecast accuracy (out-of-sample)</h2>
<table>
<tr><th class="l">Model</th><th>MAE</th><th>RMSE</th><th>MAPE</th><th>MAE / naive</th><th>DM stat</th><th>DM p</th><th>Dir. acc.</th><th>95% CI</th><th>n</th><th>p vs 50%</th></tr>
{% for name, m in r.metrics.items() %}
<tr><td class="l">{{ name }}</td><td>{{ m.mae|fmt }}</td><td>{{ m.rmse|fmt }}</td><td>{{ m.mape_pct|fmt(3) }}%</td>
<td>{{ m.rel_mae_vs_naive|fmt(4) }}</td>
<td>{{ (m.dm_vs_naive.stat if m.dm_vs_naive else None)|fmt(3) }}</td><td>{{ (m.dm_vs_naive.p_value if m.dm_vs_naive else None)|fmt(3) }}</td>
<td>{{ m.directional.accuracy|pct }}</td><td>{% if m.directional.accuracy is not none %}{{ m.directional.ci_low|pct }}&ndash;{{ m.directional.ci_high|pct }}{% else %}n/a{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ m.directional.n }}</td><td>{{ m.directional.p_value_vs_50pct|fmt(3) }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% if r.metrics_post_release %}
<h3>4b. Origins after Kronos's public release ({{ r.pretraining_shadow.public_release }}) only &mdash; {{ r.metrics_post_release.n_origins }} origins</h3>
<table>
<tr><th class="l">Model</th><th>MAE</th><th>RMSE</th><th>MAPE</th><th>Dir. acc.</th><th>95% CI</th><th>n</th><th>p vs 50%</th></tr>
{% for name, m in r.metrics_post_release.models.items() %}
<tr><td class="l">{{ name }}</td><td>{{ m.mae|fmt }}</td><td>{{ m.rmse|fmt }}</td><td>{{ m.mape_pct|fmt(3) }}%</td><td>{{ m.directional.accuracy|pct }}</td>
<td>{% if m.directional.accuracy is not none %}{{ m.directional.ci_low|pct }}&ndash;{{ m.directional.ci_high|pct }}{% else %}n/a{% endif %}</td><td>{{ m.directional.n }}</td><td>{{ m.directional.p_value_vs_50pct|fmt(3) }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% endif %}
<h3>Inference latency (measured on this run's CPU)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th class="l">Model</th><th>forecasts</th><th>p50 ms</th><th>p95 ms</th><th>mean ms</th><th>total s</th></tr>
{% for name, m in r.metrics.items() %}<tr><td class="l">{{ name }}</td><td>{{ m.latency.n }}</td><td>{{ m.latency.p50_ms|fmt(2) }}</td><td>{{ m.latency.p95_ms|fmt(2) }}</td><td>{{ m.latency.mean_ms|fmt(2) }}</td><td>{{ m.latency.total_s|fmt(2) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
<div class="muted">Hardware: {{ r.environment.hardware.cpu_model }}, {{ r.environment.hardware.logical_cpus }} logical CPUs, torch threads {{ r.environment.hardware.torch_threads }}.</div>

<h2>5. Charts (out-of-sample)</h2>
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ charts.oos_forecasts }}" alt="forecast paths">
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ charts.rolling_error }}" alt="rolling error">
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ charts.error_distribution }}" alt="error distribution">
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ charts.directional }}" alt="directional accuracy">
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ charts.latency }}" alt="latency">

<h2>6. Research backtest (historical simulation, not investment advice)</h2>
<div class="research">
Rule evaluated for each model: at each origin, take exposure equal to the sign of the model's forecast move to bar {{ r.config.horizon }}
({{ r.backtest.config.mode }}), entered {{ r.backtest.config.delay_bars }} bar(s) after the origin close and held for {{ r.config.horizon }} bars;
costs {{ r.backtest.config.cost_bps_per_side }} bps per side (sensitivity at {{ r.backtest.config.cost_sensitivity_bps|join(', ') }} bps).
No slippage model beyond the bps assumption, no funding/borrow costs, no position sizing. The section is shown only when at least
{{ r.backtest.config.min_trades }} active non-overlapping periods exist and all leakage checks pass.
</div>
<table>
<tr><th class="l">Model</th><th>Status</th><th>active / periods</th><th>gross return</th><th>net return</th><th>ann. Sharpe (net)</th><th>max DD (net)</th><th>hit rate (net)</th></tr>
{% for name, b in r.backtest.per_model.items() %}
{% if b.valid %}
<tr><td class="l">{{ name }}</td><td class="l">shown</td><td>{{ b.n_active }} / {{ b.n_periods }}</td><td>{{ b.base.total_return_gross|pct }}</td><td>{{ b.base.total_return_net|pct }}</td>
<td>{{ b.base.annualised_sharpe_net|fmt(2) }}</td><td>{{ b.base.max_drawdown_net|pct }}</td><td>{{ b.base.hit_rate_net|pct }}</td></tr>
{% else %}
<tr><td class="l">{{ name }}</td><td class="l" colspan="7">suppressed: {{ b.suppressed_reasons|join('; ') }}</td></tr>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% set ref = namespace(v=None) %}{% for name, b in r.backtest.per_model.items() %}{% if b.valid and ref.v is none %}{% set ref.v = b.passive_long_reference %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% if ref.v %}<div class="muted">Passive long reference over the same span (one round trip of costs): gross {{ ref.v.total_return_gross|pct }}, net {{ ref.v.total_return_net|pct }}.</div>{% endif %}
{% if charts.research_equity %}
<h3>Cost sensitivity (net total return)</h3>
<table><tr><th class="l">Model</th>{% for c in r.backtest.config.cost_sensitivity_bps %}<th>{{ c }} bps</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% for name, b in r.backtest.per_model.items() %}{% if b.valid %}<tr><td class="l">{{ name }}</td>{% for s in b.sensitivity %}<td>{{ s.total_return_net|pct }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
</table>
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ charts.research_equity }}" alt="research equity">
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ charts.cost_sensitivity }}" alt="cost sensitivity">
{% endif %}

<h2>7. Leakage and data-quality checks</h2>
<table>
<tr><th class="l">Check</th><th class="l">Result</th></tr>
<tr><td class="l">Fold structure (fit end &lt; target start, no overlapping windows)</td><td class="l">{{ r.leakage.structural_fold_checks }}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="l">Negative control: deliberately leaky model must be detected</td><td class="l">{{ 'detected (detector working)' if r.leakage.negative_control.detected else 'NOT detected' }}; max forecast change {{ r.leakage.negative_control.max_abs_diff|fmt }}</td></tr>
{% for inv in r.leakage.future_invariance %}
<tr><td class="l">Future-invariance: {{ inv.model }} (origins {{ inv.origins_checked|join(', ') }})</td><td class="l">{{ 'passed' if inv.passed else 'FAILED' }} (max forecast change when future bars are altered: {{ inv.max_abs_diff|fmt }})</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
<tr><td class="l">Pre-training window (Kronos)</td><td class="l">{% if r.pretraining_shadow.synthetic_data %}not applicable: synthetic data{% else %}{{ r.pretraining_shadow.targets_on_or_before_cutoff }} window(s) end on/before stated cut-off {{ r.pretraining_shadow.training_cutoff }}; {{ r.pretraining_shadow.origins_before_public_release }} origin(s) before / {{ r.pretraining_shadow.origins_after_public_release }} after public release {{ r.pretraining_shadow.public_release }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
</table>
<h3>Warnings</h3>
{% if r.warnings %}<table><tr><th class="l">Code</th><th class="l">Severity</th><th class="l">Finding</th><th class="l">Why it matters</th></tr>
{% for w in r.warnings %}<tr><td class="l">{{ w.code }}</td><td class="l sev-{{ w.severity }}">{{ w.severity }}</td><td class="l">{{ w.message }}</td><td class="l">{{ w.explanation }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>{% else %}<p>No data-quality warnings.</p>{% endif %}

<h2>8. Limitations</h2>
<ul>
<li>One instrument, one horizon, one historical period. Results may not transfer to other instruments, regimes or horizons.</li>
<li>Kronos is evaluated zero-shot with fixed sampling settings; other settings, larger variants or fine-tuning may behave differently. Its training data is not public, so contamination cannot be ruled out for periods before its release.</li>
<li>ARIMA uses a fixed order on log prices; no order search was performed.</li>
<li>Statistical tests are not adjusted for multiple comparisons across models.</li>
<li>The research backtest ignores slippage beyond the bps assumption, funding, borrow, market impact and capacity.</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Reproducibility</h2>
<table>
<tr><th class="l">Run id</th><td class="l"><code>{{ r.run_id }}</code></td><th class="l">Code commit</th><td class="l"><code>{{ r.environment.git.commit }}</code>{% if r.environment.git.dirty_src %} (uncommitted changes){% endif %}</td></tr>
<tr><th class="l">Seed</th><td class="l">{{ r.seeds.global }} (Kronos: seed + origin index)</td><th class="l">predictions.csv SHA-256</th><td class="l"><code>{{ r.artefacts['predictions.csv'] }}</code></td></tr>
<tr><th class="l">Packages</th><td class="l" colspan="3">{% for k, v in r.environment.packages.items() %}{% if v %}{{ k }} {{ v }}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
<tr><th class="l">Timings (s)</th><td class="l" colspan="3">{% for k, v in r.timings.items() %}{{ k }}={{ v|round(2) }}; {% endfor %}</td></tr>
</table>
<p class="muted">The full configuration, hashes, timings and the compute-cost estimate are in <code>manifest.json</code>. Re-run with <code>quanteval reproduce --manifest manifest.json --csv &lt;same file&gt;</code>.</p>
<p class="muted">Third-party notices: Kronos model code &copy; 2025 ShiYu, MIT License (vendored at commit 67b630e); Kronos-mini and Kronos-Tokenizer-2k weights published under MIT on Hugging Face by NeoQuasar. Citation: Shi et al., "Kronos: A Foundation Model for the Language of Financial Markets", arXiv:2508.02739.</p>
</body></html>
